67:Stage durations (from `evidence/session3_console.log`, UTC): preflight 00:02–00:04; E6 00:04–00:31 (two A/A pairs, 40 headline restarts, all eligible); E3 00:31–00:40; E2 00:40–01:52 (the two C3M traces took 30 and 25 minutes because a max-autotune trace recompiles with the Inductor caches disabled under the profiler); E1 01:52–02:36 (C3F, C3G, C3P with their traces and SDR gates); E9 02:36–02:48; E4a 02:48–04:00; E5 04:00–04:30; E7 04:30–04:31; collection and audit 04:31.
75:See the summary table in §1; the verdict lines with the exact rule applied are in `SESSION3_RESULT.md` ("Registered prediction" lines). The E9 registration (`docs/phase3/e9/e9_cost_model.json`, sha256 recorded in `session3_config.json` at session start) predicted the crossover at 261,072 samples; the measurement puts it between 264,600 and 352,800. Under the registered rule the residual is attributed, not refitted: absorbing it in one term would require C3's per-band GEMM rate to be 53 rather than 71 TFLOPS at 401 frames and 67 rather than 82 at 601 (`docs/phase3/e9/e9_residual.json`), i.e. the two-point saturating rate curves are wrong at mid lengths, consistent with the in-sample residual of −0.42 ms at 88,200.
83:On-pod: COMPLETE 198/198, evidence grade pod, no optional item incomplete. Codex gate 10 (`docs/codex/10_analysis.md`, findings 139–150, ANALYSIS-READY: no) then found that the publishers ignored the audit's clock flags, that the E6 items did not enforce the registered 5 % rule, that the extern-GEMM count included Triton templates, and that E2's gain had been attributed in part to cast fusion that the C3M traces contradict, plus eight eligibility and missing-input defects; all twelve were closed in the analysis tools with recorded identity (every publisher now goes through one reducer that validates the record, joins the manifest, recomputes differences from samples by repeat and excludes clock-flagged repeats). The corrected re-audit (`session_status_reaudit_gate10.json`) is INCOMPLETE 195/199: the tree-identity item (inapplicable off-pod) and the three compiled 100 ms headline cells (C3, H, C1), whose SM clock varied 2572–2992 MHz across restarts; those headlines are published clock-flagged, and every 100 ms pair value uses clock-clean repeats. The 8 s results are unaffected. No measuring code was changed after the session.
